------------------------------- Standard Mode ----------------------------------------------------

- Start with deploying this github repo as first E-Commerce App Project  :- 

1. https://github.com/LondheShubham153/elastic-beanstalk-in-one-shot/blob/main/projects/project-1-single-tier.md
2. Source 
3. Clone the repo locally on your system not on EC2 instance :- git clone https://github.com/LondheShubham153/e-commerce-github-actions.git
4. Go to Project-1/beanstalk/docker-compose.yml file pls compressed it to the zip file.
5. Choose .zip file from local when creating the Standard Mode Environment in elasticbeanstalk.
6. Platform-Specific-Options -> Proxy Server -> Select nginx
7. Server Access -> 
- Service Role -> Use another role -> select role -> aws-elasticbeanstalk-service-role
- EC2 instance profile -> Use another role -> select role -> aws-elasticbeanstalk-ec2-role
- EC2 key pair -> eb-server-key (if u want to do ssh on this server)

- Then click on Create.

Note :-
- U can see the application will be deployed and can be accessible by ur domain that u provided so the moral of the thing is that if u have a dockerfile of ur application so u can easily deploy that.
- Dockerfile se banti ha Docker Image and -> Docker Image se banta ha Docker container.
- The best thing is that we don't need to write any yml or manifest file for it.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- We can also deploy the app via the CLI so to follow this :- 
https://github.com/LondheShubham153/elastic-beanstalk-in-one-shot/blob/main/projects/project-1-single-tier.md
- Run it with the EB CLI

------------------------------- Cluster Mode ----------------------------------------------------
. Again entering the details of app like name :- e-commerce-store-app-cluster and provide ur desired domain name :- 
hascolabs-cluster.
. and Copy the docker image command from the :- https://hub.docker.com/r/trainwithshubham/e-commerce-python
. Select Application Code :- Container Image
. Container Image URI :- trainwithshubham/e-commerce-python:latest
. Service Port :- 8080
. Service Role :- U can create the new role and select the existing role as defined in Standard Mode Demo part above.

